Task 1: Initialize Git Repository & Add Maven Project Files (5 Marks)
bash
# Navigate to your project directory
cd /path/to/your/maven-project

# Initialize Git repository
git init

# Add all Maven project files to staging
git add .

# Verify files are staged (optional)
git status
Task 2: Set Global Config & Push to GitHub (5 Marks)
bash
# Set global Git configuration
git config --global user.name "saiivignesh21"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"

# Verify global config (optional)
git config --global --list

# Create initial commit
git commit -m "Initial commit: Add Maven project files"

# Add remote origin (replace with your actual repo URL)
git remote add origin https://github.com/saiivignesh21/SE-lab.git

# Verify remote is added (optional)
git remote -v

# Push to GitHub (main branch)
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
Task 3: Create Feature Branch Tracking Remote (4 Marks)
bash
# Create and switch to new local branch that tracks remote
git checkout -b feature/engine-update --track origin/feature/engine-update

# OR alternatively:
git checkout --track origin/feature/engine-update

# Make your initial changes/commit
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit on feature/engine-update branch"

# Push to GitHub (creates the remote branch)
git push -u origin feature/engine-update

# Verify branch tracking (optional)
git branch -vv
Task 4: Stash Work, Fix Hotfix, Return to Work
This scenario uses git stash to temporarily save incomplete work:

bash
# You're on feature branch with incomplete CarController.java changes
# Stash your incomplete work (saves it safely)
git stash

# Switch to main branch to apply hotfix
git checkout main

# Create hotfix branch (optional but recommended)
git checkout -b hotfix/critical-bug

# Fix the critical bug
# Edit and save your files...
git add .
git commit -m "Hotfix: Resolve critical bug"

# Push hotfix to GitHub
git push -u origin hotfix/critical-bug

# Switch back to your feature branch
git checkout feature/engine-update

# Restore your stashed work
git stash pop

# Continue editing CarController.java
# When ready, commit your work
git add .
git commit -m "Complete CarController implementation"
git push origin feature/engine-update
Quick Reference - Complete Workflow
bash
# 1. Clone (if not done)
git clone https://github.com/saiivignesh21/SE-lab.git
cd SE-lab

# 2. Copy your Maven project files here

# 3. Initialize and push
git config --global user.name "saiivignesh21"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit: Add Maven project"
git remote add origin https://github.com/saiivignesh21/SE-lab.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main

# 4. Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature/engine-update
git push -u origin feature/engine-update

# 5. Stash scenario
git stash                          # Save incomplete work
git checkout main                  # Switch to main
git checkout -b hotfix/bug-fix     # Create hotfix
# ... fix bug ...
git add . && git commit -m "Fix bug"
git push origin hotfix/bug-fix
git checkout feature/engine-update # Back to feature
git stash pop                       # Restore work
# ... continue ...
git add . && git commit -m "Complete work"
git push origin feature/engine-update
Tips:

Make sure Maven project files (pom.xml, src/, target/) are in the directory before git add .
Use git status frequently to verify your changes
The -u flag in git push -u sets upstream tracking for the branch
git stash list shows all stashed changes
git stash show -p shows stash contents before applying
